import ../../../ui/scene_draws.dl
import ../../../ui/scene_surfaces.dl

to get [a test scene object named] {a value:name} [using] {UI scene mesh:mesh} [at depth] {floating-point number:depth} [mirrored] {boolean:mirrored} [transparent] {boolean:transparent}:
    set material to a UI scene material with color (UI ink 200 120 80) roughness 0.8 metalness 0.0
    if transparent:
        set material's opacity to 0.5
        set material's double sided to true
        set material's depth write to false
    set pose to an identity UI scene pose
    set pose's position's z to depth
    if mirrored:
        set pose's scale's x to -1.0
    set part to a UI scene mesh part named "body" under -1 using mesh with material material at pose
    return a UI scene object named name with model (a UI scene model from [part])

to [check stable scene sorting]:
    set records to an empty list of UI scene ordered record
    set scratch to an empty list of UI scene ordered record
    loop index from 0 to 257:
        set record to a new UI scene ordered record
        set record's depth to ((index * 73) % 23) as a floating-point number
        store (index as a 32 bit unsigned integer) into record's record's flags at 0
        append record to records
    sort UI scene records records using scratch
    set previous to 100.0
    set serial to 0 as a 32 bit unsigned integer
    for each record in records:
        set current to the item at 0 in record's record's flags
        require condition (record's depth <= previous) reporting "Scene depth sorting did not order an irregular non-power-of-two input"
        if record's depth = previous:
            require condition (current > serial) reporting "Equal-depth transparent instances lost their stable source order"
        set previous to record's depth
        set serial to current
    free records
    free scratch

set bank to a UI scene mesh bank
set frame to a UI scene frame using bank
set mesh to a UI box mesh with 1 by 1 by 1 segments
set opaque to a test scene object named "opaque" using mesh at depth 1.0 mirrored false transparent false
set near to a test scene object named "near" using mesh at depth 2.0 mirrored false transparent true
set far to a test scene object named "far" using mesh at depth 0.0 mirrored true transparent true
set objects to a list containing opaque
append near to objects
append far to objects
set camera to a UI scene camera at (a UI scene vector from [0.0,0.0,5.0]) aimed at (a UI scene vector from [0.0,0.0,0.0]) with angle 35.0 aspect 1.0 near 0.1 far 100.0
prepare UI scene frame frame from objects through camera
require condition ((bank's revision = 1) and ((the length of bank's vertices) = 24)) reporting "Objects with shared geometry created duplicate GPU streams"
require condition (((the length of frame's records) = 3) and ((the length of frame's draws) = 3)) reporting "Scene frame dropped mixed-pipeline instances"
require condition (((the item at 0 in frame's draws)'s pipeline = 0) and (((the item at 1 in frame's draws)'s pipeline = 15) and ((the item at 2 in frame's draws)'s pipeline = 14))) reporting "Transparent draws lost global back-to-front ordering"
require condition ((the item at 14 in (the item at 1 in frame's records)'s matrix) = 0.0) reporting "Far transparent object was not submitted first"
require condition ((the item at 14 in (the item at 2 in frame's records)'s matrix) = 2.0) reporting "Near transparent object was not submitted last"
require condition ((the length of frame's shadow records) = 3) reporting "Color depth-write settings suppressed shadow casters"
require condition (((the item at 0 in frame's shadow draws)'s pipeline = 0) and (((the item at 1 in frame's shadow draws)'s pipeline = 2) and ((the item at 2 in frame's shadow draws)'s pipeline = 3))) reporting "Shadow draws did not preserve mirroring and two-sided faces independently of blending"
set revision to far's revision
prepare UI scene frame frame from objects through camera
require condition ((far's revision = revision) and (bank's revision = 1)) reporting "Unchanged objects repacked transforms or reuploaded meshes"
set tint to linear UI ink red 0.5 green 0.75 blue 1.0
set UI scene color multiplier in far to tint
prepare UI scene frame frame from objects through camera
set colored to the item at 1 in (frame's records)
set original to linear UI ink from (UI ink 200 120 80)
require condition ((the absolute value of ((the item at 0 in (colored's color)) - original's red * 0.5)) < 0.00001) reporting "Instance tint did not multiply in linear color space"
set revision to far's revision
set UI scene color multiplier in far to tint
prepare UI scene frame frame from objects through camera
require condition (far's revision = revision) reporting "An unchanged linear color multiplier invalidated cached instances"
set UI scene color multiplier in far to (linear UI ink red 1.0 green 1.0 blue 1.0)
set duplicate to a test scene object named "opaque" using mesh at depth -1.0 mirrored false transparent false
append duplicate to objects
prepare UI scene frame frame from objects through camera
require condition (((the length of frame's draws) = 3) and ((the item at 0 in frame's draws)'s instances = 2)) reporting "Opaque instances using one mesh and state were not batched"
remove the last item from objects
set pose to an identity UI scene pose
set pose's position's x to 7.0
set UI scene root pose in (duplicate's instance) to pose
set replacement to a UI scene model from [a UI scene mesh part named "changed" under -1 using mesh with material (a UI scene material with color (UI ink 10 20 30) roughness 0.2 metalness 0.5) at (an identity UI scene pose)]
set UI scene model in duplicate to replacement
refresh UI scene object duplicate
require condition ((duplicate's instance's model's parts' data = replacement's parts' data) and ((the item at 12 in (the item at 0 in duplicate's packets)'s record's matrix) = 7.0)) reporting "Replacing a model lost shared geometry or the object transform"
close UI scene object duplicate
set viewport to UI box at 0.0 0.0 sized 100.0 100.0
set ray to the UI scene ray at (a UI point at 50.0 and 50.0) through camera in viewport
set selected to the UI scene object selection from ray among objects including backfaces false
require condition ((selected's object = near) and (selected's selection's part = 0)) reporting "Picking did not select the nearest rendered object"
set near's pickable to false
set selected to the UI scene object selection from ray among objects including backfaces false
require condition (selected's object = opaque) reporting "Object pickability was ignored"
set opaque's visible to false
set pose to far's instance's root pose
set pose's position's z to 3.0
set UI scene root pose in (far's instance) to pose
prepare UI scene frame frame from objects through camera
require condition (((the length of frame's records) = 2) and ((the item at 0 in frame's draws)'s pipeline = 14)) reporting "Visibility or changed transforms did not update ordering"
require condition (far's revision > revision) reporting "Changed objects did not refresh their cached records"
set pipelines to the UI scene color pipelines
set shadows to the UI scene shadow pipelines
require condition ((pipelines's length = 16) and (shadows's length = 4)) reporting "Scene raster variants are incomplete"
set state to the JSON value at index 15 in pipelines
require condition (((the JSON text named "frontFace" in state) = "cw") and (((the JSON text named "cullMode" in state) = "none") and ((the JSON boolean named "depthWrite" in state) = false))) reporting "Mirrored translucent two-sided material selected the wrong raster state"
free pipelines
free shadows
close UI scene frame frame
close UI scene mesh bank bank
# Reuse cached objects with a different bank: cached packets must not retain atlas offsets.
set bank to a UI scene mesh bank
set unused to the span of UI mesh (a UI plane mesh with 1 by 1 segments) in bank
set frame to a UI scene frame using bank
prepare UI scene frame frame from objects through camera
require condition (((the item at 0 in frame's draws)'s first = 6) and ((the item at 0 in frame's draws)'s vertex offset = 4)) reporting "Object caches retained offsets into a previous mesh bank"
close UI scene frame frame
close UI scene mesh bank bank
for each object in objects:
    close UI scene object object
free objects
check stable scene sorting
print line "Scene submission caches shared objects, batches opaque geometry, orders transparency, preserves shadow states and selects rendered instances."
